lture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $441K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $142K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Dropbox, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $7.2B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +9.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 80% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $931M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 37 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.87\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 6.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 23.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 8.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (29.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $45.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 60% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 28% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dropbox, Inc. $DBX Position Lowered by Illinois Municipal Retirement Fund","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/dropbox-inc-dbx-position-lowered-by-illinois-municipal-retirement-fund.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794560829.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.852,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dropbox (NASDAQ:DBX) Given New $36.00 Price Target at JPMorgan C